{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.lt_of_b4_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.lt_of_b4_pos","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L175-L180","doc":"**`b₄ > 0` is convexity at `z = 1`**, i.e. the *rise* itself accelerates:\nthe step from coordination 2 to 3 is larger than the step from 1 to 2. Measured,\nboth hold — `Δw 1 = 0.475` and `Δw 2 = 2.016 MeV` per pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.not_le_of_b3_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.not_le_of_b3_pos","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L169-L173","doc":"Restated as the refutation of a hypothesis class: `b₃ > 0` rules out every\nassembly whose coordination weight is non-increasing at the bottom of the\nladder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.lt_of_b3_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.lt_of_b3_pos","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L158-L167","doc":"**The falsifiable form**, and the one measurement instantiates.\n\nAME2020 gives `b₃ = +1.426222 MeV > 0` (Ursell inversion of the deuteron and the\nisospin-averaged `A = 3` binding). So the physical coordination weight **rises**\nfrom coordination 1 to coordination 2: `w 1 < w 2`. That single inequality is\nthe entire content of \"nature's `b₃` is positive\", and it is what a derivation\nof the magnitude has to produce. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b3_nonpos_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b3_nonpos_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L144-L156","doc":"**A non-increasing coordination weight forces `b₃ ≤ 0`.**\n\nThis is the wall, and it subsumes the Mayer result rather than sitting beside\nit: any assembly whose mean binding per pair does not *rise* with coordination\ngives a non-positive connected three-body cumulant. A saturating assembly is\nnon-increasing, so it lands here — the multiplicative form's `b₃ < 0` is an\ninstance, not a coincidence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b4_eq_zero_of_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b4_eq_zero_of_const","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L132-L136","doc":"And the four-body cumulant likewise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b3_eq_zero_of_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b3_eq_zero_of_const","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L123-L130","doc":"**The pairwise wall, recovered.** A constant coordination weight — which is\nwhat a pairwise-additive assembly with a transferable bond is — has vanishing\nconnected three-body cumulant. This is\n`QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.b3_eq_zero_of_isPairwise` as the `Δw = 0`\ncase; the point is that it is no longer a separate fact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b4_eq_diff_of_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b4_eq_diff_of_diff","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L117-L121","doc":"The second difference, written as a difference of differences, so that the\n`bₙ = C(n,2)·Δ^{n-2}w 1` shape is visible at `n = 4` too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b4_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b4_eq","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L111-L115","doc":"**`b₄` is six times the second difference.** The `6` is `C(4,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b3_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b3_eq","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L105-L109","doc":"**`b₃` is three times the first difference of the coordination weight.**\nThe `3` is `C(3,2)`, the number of pairs in a triple. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.bind_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.bind_zero","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L102-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.bind_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.bind_one","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L97-L100","doc":"A one-body and a bare nucleon carry no pairs, so the inversion may run from\n`k = 0` without changing anything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b4","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L94-L95","doc":"The **connected four-body cumulant**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.b3","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L90-L92","doc":"The **connected three-body cumulant**, by Möbius inversion over the subset\nlattice with `bind _ 0 = bind _ 1 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.fwdDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.fwdDiff","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L87-L88","doc":"The **forward difference** `Δw z = w (z+1) - w z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.bind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationWeightDifferences.bind","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationWeightDifferences.lean#L81-L85","doc":"The **coordination weight** assembly: a nucleus of mass number `A` carries\n`C(A,2)` pairs, each contributing the mean weight `w (A-1)` of a nucleon at\ncoordination `z = A-1`. Every binding map is of this form for exactly one `w`;\nthis is a change of variables, not a hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}